"GB","home":false,"pf":17.0,"pa":41.0,"off_snaps":57,"epa_per_play":-0.1917,"pass_rate":0.6491,"pass_rate_neutral":0.6154,"def_epa_per_play":0.1115},{"week":18,"opponent":"CHI","home":false,"pf":29.0,"pa":13.0,"off_snaps":71,"epa_per_play":0.2517,"pass_rate":0.4648,"pass_rate_neutral":0.4783,"def_epa_per_play":-0.1569}],"comps":{"offense":[{"season":2025,"team":"DAL","distance":0.6875,"shared":21,"play_caller":"Brian Schottenheimer"},{"season":2025,"team":"DEN","distance":0.706,"shared":21,"play_caller":"Sean Payton"},{"season":2022,"team":"LAC","distance":0.7111,"shared":24,"play_caller":null},{"season":2023,"team":"LV","distance":0.7435,"shared":21,"play_caller":null},{"season":2022,"team":"LA","distance":0.774,"shared":24,"play_caller":"Sean McVay"}],"defense":[{"season":2018,"team":"CHI","distance":0.5351,"shared":18,"play_caller":"Vic Fangio"},{"season":2019,"team":"DEN","distance":0.7169,"shared":18,"play_caller":"Vic Fangio"},{"season":2019,"team":"CHI","distance":0.7194,"shared":18,"play_caller":null},{"season":2025,"team":"SF","distance":0.8138,"shared":22,"play_caller":"Robert Saleh"},{"season":2020,"team":"CHI","distance":0.8682,"shared":18,"play_caller":null}]},"overview":{"overview":"The Vikings went 13-4 in 2022 and were outscored 427 to 424. The offense ranked 19th in EPA per play and the defense 21st in EPA allowed, so neither side stood out much. That record was better than the underlying numbers, which suggests a few close games went their way. Their most distinctive traits were a neutral-script pass rate that was among the highest and the 2nd highest Cover 6 rate in the league.","offense":"The Vikings offense was a little below average by EPA per play, and it was much better passing the ball than running it. They threw more than almost anyone relative to the situation, even when the score did not call for it. Schematically, they stood out for a shotgun rate that was among the lowest and the 3rd highest under center rate in the league. Kirk Cousins ran the passing game and leaned heavily on Justin Jefferson, who drew 29% of the targets.","defense":"The Vikings defense was a little below average by EPA allowed per play. Its strongest area was takeaways per game, where it ranked 10th, and its weakest was success rate allowed, where it ranked 26th. D.J. Wonnum was as productive as expected, but the bigger surprise was Za'Darius Smith, who had 10 sacks, after not being a regular on this defense last season. In terms of scheme, they had the 2nd highest Cover 6 rate in the league.","special":"The Vikings were about average in how often they went for it on fourth down. Their kickers made 79% of field goals, which was well below average. On the roster side, they put an unusually large share of their salary cap into linebackers, about 19% of the money on the books.","players":"Kirk Cousins played nearly every snap at quarterback and threw for 4,547 yards. Justin Jefferson was the clear top target with 29% of the looks and 1,809 receiving yards. Dalvin Cook handled most of the work in the backfield with 72% of the carries. On defense, Danielle Hunter led the team with 10.5 sacks and Patrick Peterson picked off 5 passes.","coaching":"Kevin O'Connell called the offense, and the defensive play caller for this season is not in the coaching data. Their offense looked most like the 2025 Cowboys under Brian Schottenheimer and the 2025 Broncos under Sean Payton. Their defense looked most like the 2018 Bears and the 2019 Broncos, both under Vic Fangio.","trends":"The offense went from 16th in EPA per play in 2021 to 19th in 2022, a modest decline. The defense moved from 12th in EPA allowed per play in 2021 to 21st in 2022, a big step back. The biggest change in approach was 11 personnel usage, which went from 44% to 74%.","notes":"2022 is the first season with every data source available, including FTN's play design charting. It is also the last season that used the older formation labels, so singleback and I formation rates still appear here."}}